+      <h2>ADK Training Portal</h2>
+      <p>When you sign in to the ADK training portal with Google, we receive your Google account identifier, verified email address, and display name. Your instructor manually approves access and controls when modules and solutions become available. We use an essential session cookie to keep you signed in for up to 12 hours.</p>
+      <p>For approved learners, the portal records pages visited, visit times, last activity, and estimated active time. Active-time tracking pauses when the page is hidden or unfocused, or after five minutes without interaction. It does not record keystroke contents or screen recordings, and it is not proof that a page was read. The instructor can view and export these reports to support teaching.</p>
+      <p>Portal records are stored separately in Cloudflare D1. Activity and administrative audit records are retained for 90 days and removed by scheduled cleanup. Access approval and account records remain until they are removed; revoking access does not automatically delete the learner's retained activity. Contact Inder using the details below to request deletion. Existing public GitHub resources remain independently accessible and are not included in portal activity reports.</p>
