+---
+Status: SPEC-APPROVED
+Feature: ADK training portal integration
+Approval: User explicitly requested implementation of the agreed portal plan.
+---
+
+# ADK training portal integration
+
+Add an ADK Training link to shared site navigation, pointing to
+`https://gyanhq.com/adk-training/`, and describe the portal's identity/session
+and learner-activity processing in the existing privacy page.
+
+The training repository owns the separate Worker, D1 database, authentication,
+manual approval, module/solution release controls, and 90-day activity reports.
+The GyanHQ marketing site keeps its vanilla HTML/CSS/JS architecture. Its
+registration and blog APIs, KV bindings, email setup, and deployment remain
+unchanged. No build dependency or new backend is added to this repository.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- The shared navigation link works on desktop and mobile without overflow.
+- Existing registration dialog, program pages, and blog catalogue remain usable.
+- Privacy text explains Google identity, the essential 12-hour session cookie,
+  page visits/estimated active time, five-minute idle cutoff, 90-day retention,
+  administrator reporting/export, and deletion contact.
+- Keep this patch off production until the training Worker's staging checks and
+  narrowly scoped production routing are ready. Rollback reverses this patch.
+
+## Validation
+
+17 existing registration backend tests pass. 50 browser checks pass across the
+home, program, instructor, blogs, and privacy pages at 390/900/1440px, including
+navigation, registration-dialog, blog-reader, and privacy-notice checks.
